
==========================================================================
  QS_n DUMMY-REGISTER SIMULATOR  (concrete n = 2, A = Q)
==========================================================================

Builds the fixed-order dummy-register simulator of QS_n at n = 2,
concrete f_1 = X, f_2 = H. Type:
  (Bool ⊗ Bool) ⊗ (Q ⊗ (Q ⊗ Q))  ⟶  (Bool ⊗ Bool) ⊗ (Q ⊗ (Q ⊗ Q))

  Control  (C_1, C_2) : Bool ⊗ Bool     (2 tag qubits)
  Regs     T ⊗ (D_1 ⊗ D_2) : Q ⊗ (Q⊗Q)  (target + 2 dummies, 3 qubits)
  Total    5 qubits.

  Circuit: R(C_1) ; F ; R(C_1) ; R(C_2) ; F ; R(C_2)
  with routing rearrangements between rounds (0-gate wire perms).
  R(c) is a coherent controlled-SWAP of T with D_c (via case_hom).
  F applies X to D_1 and H to D_2 in parallel (leaves T alone).

==========================================================================
