  compiled successfully (gate count: 2)

round(c)  = R(c) ; F ; R(c):
  compiled successfully (gate count: 10)

qs2_sim  (full two-round pipeline):
  compiled successfully (gate count: 20)

==========================================================================
  PART 2: Structural involutions
==========================================================================

  ✓ R ; R  =  id_{Bool ⊗ Regs}  (controlled-SWAP squared) (fidelity=1.000000)
  ✓ round ; round  =  id  (each round is an involution: X² = H² = I) (fidelity=1.000000)

==========================================================================
  PART 3: Clean-garbage lemma (dummies factor out)
==========================================================================

The defining semantic claim of the dummy-register construction:
on every basis (c_1, c_2), the dummies pick up f_i^{n-1} independent
of π. For n = 2, f_1 = X, f_2 = H:

  (c_1, c_2) = (0, 0):  identity on Regs   (X² = H² = I on doubly-hit)
  (c_1, c_2) = (0, 1):  target ← H·X ψ,   D_1 ← X a_1,  D_2 ← H a_2
  (c_1, c_2) = (1, 0):  target ← X·H ψ,   D_1 ← X a_1,  D_2 ← H a_2
  (c_1, c_2) = (1, 1):  identity on Regs

  qs2_ref encodes this specification as a nested case on (c_1, c_2).
  If the dummies genuinely factor out (i.e., they carry no π-dependent
  information), qs2_sim MUST equal qs2_ref as a full 5-qubit unitary.


qs2_ref  (nested-case specification):
  compiled successfully (gate count: 12)
  ✓ qs2_sim  =  qs2_ref  (clean-garbage lemma; π-independent dummies) (fidelity=1.000000)

==========================================================================
  SUMMARY
==========================================================================

  Verifications: 3/3 passed

Demonstrated: the QS_2 higher-order n-switch is faithfully
simulated by a first-order dummy-register circuit with n² = 4
oracle calls. Under η-expansion of the target, the whole term
is first-order (no sum type carries a function payload), so the
soundness restriction is respected. The dummies genuinely factor
out — proved as a unitary equality between the operational
circuit (qs2_sim) and the semantic reference (qs2_ref).

The fully-parametric form (each f_i as an abstract function value)
is obtained by wrapping qs2_sim's shape in an outer olam over four
(Q ⊸ Q) function slots and replacing each concrete gate site with
an oapp of the corresponding slot. See qswitch_eta_endoQ_e2e.ml
for the destructuring / split-witness pattern.
